{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,15.359,1.643,1.471,"India Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"12 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,31.015,3.651,3.268,"Glass Wall Systems"],[13.889,14.731,48.734,2.373,2.124,"H2 is in the order book; FY28 needs US orders back"],[13.889,20.845,52.951,1.809,1.634,"Glass Wall Systems builds façades in India and exports them, mainly to the US."],[13.889,22.289,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Q2 FY27 PAT rose 31% y/y to ₹28.6 cr on revenue of ₹131.5 cr (+3%), helped"],[13.889,23.733,52.931,1.809,1.634,"by two items. EBITDA of ₹37.5 cr (28.5% margin) included ₹6 cr of escalation"],[13.889,25.177,52.931,1.809,1.634,"claims for costs booked earlier; without them the margin was 25.1%. Revenue"],[13.889,26.621,52.954,1.809,1.634,"included ₹9 cr of export freight now billed to customers; net of it, sales fell 4%"],[13.889,28.065,52.934,1.809,1.634,"in Q2 and rose 9% in H1. Guidance was called unchanged, yet ‘around 25%’"],[13.889,29.509,46.763,1.809,1.634,"growth on the October call became 20-22% net of freight in November."],[13.889,31.995,52.964,1.809,1.634,"H2 should be strong as three export projects ship. We forecast H2 revenue of"],[13.889,33.439,52.936,1.809,1.634,"₹340 cr (+36%) and FY27E revenue of ₹579 cr, up 18.4% net of freight and just"],[13.889,34.883,52.934,1.809,1.634,"under guidance, at a 24.5% EBITDA margin, for EPS of ₹12.38. FY28 is less"],[13.889,36.328,52.931,1.809,1.634,"visible. The order book slipped from over ₹1,000 cr in June to ₹957 cr; the"],[13.889,37.772,52.931,1.809,1.634,"export book was ₹186 cr in July against FY26 export revenue of ₹207 cr, and"],[13.889,39.216,52.931,1.809,1.634,"US developers are deferring awards. Without new export orders we estimate"],[13.889,40.684,52.934,1.809,1.634,"only ₹30-60 cr of that book is left by March. We assume ₹420 cr of H2 orders"],[13.889,42.128,33.711,1.809,1.634,"and revenue growth of 18% and 16% in FY28-29E."],[13.889,44.59,52.931,1.809,1.634,"The shares, up 34% on the ₹182 IPO price, trade at 19.7x FY27E and 17.5x"],[13.889,46.034,52.931,1.809,1.634,"FY28E EPS; four listed building peers with c.10% EBITDA margins trade at a"],[13.889,47.502,52.961,1.809,1.634,"13x forward median. Our Dec-27 target of ₹255 averages 16x forward EPS"],[13.889,48.946,52.964,1.809,1.634,"(midpoint of today’s 18x and peers) and an FCFE DCF of ₹256 (12% cost of"],[13.889,50.39,52.931,1.809,1.634,"equity, 5.5% terminal growth). No debt, ₹114 cr of net cash and a 39% FY26"],[13.889,51.834,52.951,1.809,1.634,"ROE support the premium. We rate the shares Neutral (ladder: −5% to +15%)."],[13.889,53.278,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Upside risk: US awards resume. Downside risks: claims-led margins, share"],[13.889,54.722,52.934,1.809,1.634,"supply (a pre-IPO fund trust owns 9.4%, AIFs 12.9%; the IPO was 86% offer for"],[13.889,56.167,44.342,1.809,1.634,"sale) and a ₹33 cr sales-tax demand before the Bombay High Court."],[13.889,58.654,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[15.268,68.023,1.489,1.022,0.915,"150"],[15.268,66.066,1.489,1.022,0.915,"200"],[15.268,64.109,1.489,1.022,0.915,"250"],[15.268,62.152,1.489,1.022,0.915,"300"],[15.268,60.195,1.489,1.022,0.915,"350"],[17.147,68.717,2.96,1.022,0.915,"16 Sep"],[21.313,68.717,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[31.556,68.717,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Nov 26"],[16.416,69.888,4.899,1.275,1.111,"Glass Wall ("],[21.318,69.914,0.618,1.241,1.111,"₹"],[21.931,69.888,0.303,1.275,1.111,")"],[25.015,69.888,10.689,1.275,1.111,"NIFTY 50 (rebased to IPO)"],[20.516,71.048,1.691,1.387,1.209,"IPO"],[24.236,71.048,2.635,1.387,1.209,"Day 1"],[30.676,71.048,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[35.09,71.048,1.323,1.387,1.209,"1w"],[15.277,72.114,1.691,1.387,1.209,"Abs"],[19.322,72.114,2.811,1.387,1.209,"34.0%"],[23.99,72.114,2.811,1.387,1.209,"13.5%"],[29.42,72.114,2.597,1.387,1.209,"-8.9%"],[33.742,72.114,2.597,1.387,1.209,"-0.3%"],[15.492,73.179,1.476